<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 60,450 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 60,450 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 60,450 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7.00 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday compared to 52,593 tonnes in the same period on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>						Tuesday     September 9</p>
<p>    Export cargo			   2,054	8,660</p>
<p>    Import cargo			  58,396     43,933</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, six were expected to sail and eight were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,500	 Maribell	     10/9</p>
<p>Palm oil		 17,500	 Antea		  11/9</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
